  "prompt": "Build v4 Mosaic Switch from photo-ocean and photo-dusk. The initial pose has 21 exact 25×25px dusk crops over the ocean, starting at column 7 in row 0 and expanding diagonally to columns 2–7 in row 5; preserve every captured photo offset. Live native rendering uses the full 8×6 photographic tile field with the original 8×8 Bayer thresholds, origin-distance wave, .085 progress response, interrupted direction and 28% threshold shrink. Keep both complete photographs at the endpoints. The complete original 6px average-color tile model and all typed tile data remain intact underneath; full retains photo-archGrid/image A and photo-ocean/image B in its 400×432px composition with both credits readable. Click/touch sets the origin and switches, arrows move it, Home centers, Space/Enter switch and Escape restores A. Shell actions switch and restore A. Credit Michael Benz, JOHN TOWNER and Christophe Laurenceau. Use a 240×168 hero plane with the exact 200×150px image frame at (86,28) in the 372×264 stage: 14px corners, the supplied shadow and unchanged original SVG roots without width/height overrides. Full fields retain their original 368×268px geometry in a readable 400px-wide scroll camera. Prefix classes with rootClass and place controls in the shell. Preserve every original numerical model, typed buffer, image dataset, input rule, interruption and paint cap. Support scaled mouse coordinates, native keys and vertical touch scrolling, independent caller/viewport holds, queued intent and full cleanup. Keep the exact captured first pose until interaction, then use interruptible 150ms opacity feedback into the live model. Reduced motion keeps static feedback and disables ambient loops. Portable exports embed both Geist families, approved 800px photography and every photo credit/licence comment; local full views use their 1600px sources.",
